# Said under the greyed Earlier versions card.
common-snap-no-snapper = Las versiones anteriores necesitan snapper, que no está instalado en este equipo.

# Said under the greyed Earlier versions card.
common-snap-from-snapshot = No mientras el equipo está iniciado desde una instantánea.

# Said under the greyed Earlier versions card.
common-snap-part-of-system = La carpeta personal forma parte del sistema en este equipo, no es una parte propia del disco, así que no se pueden guardar versiones anteriores aparte del sistema.

# Said under the greyed Earlier versions card.
common-snap-network = La carpeta personal está en otro equipo, así que aquí no se pueden guardar versiones anteriores.

# Said under the greyed Earlier versions card: { $fs } is the kind of file system, such as ext4.
common-snap-not-btrfs = Las versiones anteriores necesitan la carpeta personal en Btrfs, y aquí está en { $fs }.

# Said under the greyed Earlier versions card.
common-snap-not-whole = Tu carpeta personal está dentro de otra parte del disco, no en una parte propia, así que Trindle no puede guardar versiones anteriores de ella.

# Said under the greyed Earlier versions card.
common-snap-read-only = Ahora mismo no se puede escribir en la carpeta personal, así que no se puede guardar nada.

# Said under the greyed Earlier versions card.
common-snap-locked-files = Aquí la carpeta personal se guarda como un solo archivo bloqueado, y una copia suya cada día llenaría el disco.

# Said under the greyed Earlier versions card.
common-snap-elsewhere = Tu carpeta personal no está dentro de /home, donde se hacen las copias.

# Said under the greyed Earlier versions card.
common-snap-apart = Tu carpeta personal está bloqueada o guardada aparte de las demás, así que las copias no pueden incluirla.

# Said under the greyed Earlier versions card.
common-snap-own-part = Tu carpeta personal es una parte propia del disco, en la que no entran las copias de /home.

# Why a plugin's port line in plugin.ini is refused. { $text } is what was written.
common-firewall-not-protocol-port = "{ $text }" no está escrito como protocolo:puerto, por ejemplo tcp:24810.

# Why a plugin's port line in plugin.ini is refused. { $text } is what was written before the colon.
common-firewall-bad-protocol = "{ $text }" no es tcp ni udp. Escríbelo en minúsculas.

# Why a plugin's port line in plugin.ini is refused. { $text } is what was written, { $lowest } the lowest port allowed.
common-firewall-bad-port = "{ $text }" no es un puerto de { $lowest } a 65535.

# Said when a port you open by hand isn't written as protocol:port.
common-firewall-own-form = Escríbelo como protocolo:puerto, por ejemplo tcp:37666.

# Said when a port you open by hand starts with something other than tcp or udp.
common-firewall-own-protocol = Usa tcp o udp.

# Said when a port you open by hand isn't a number from 1 to 65535.
common-firewall-own-port = Eso no es un puerto de 1 a 65535.

# Joins the last port to the others in a list of ports. { $first } is the others, comma separated.
common-firewall-and = { $first } y { $last }

# Heads a list of ports. { $count } is how many, { $list } is the ports, such as TCP 24810 and UDP 24811.
common-firewall-ports =
    { $count ->
        [one] Puerto { $list }
       *[other] Puertos { $list }
    }

# Why a plugin's ports are refused. { $max } is the most it may name.
common-firewall-too-many = Un complemento puede nombrar como máximo { $max } puertos.

# Why a plugin's ports are refused. { $port } is a port such as TCP 24810.
common-firewall-twice = { $port } aparece dos veces.

# Why a plugin's ports are refused. { $port } is a port such as TCP 80, { $lowest } the lowest allowed.
common-firewall-too-low = { $port } está por debajo de { $lowest }. Esos puertos están reservados para el sistema.

# Why a plugin's port is refused. { $port } is the number.
common-firewall-reserved = El puerto { $port } lo usa Trindle o un servicio común, así que un complemento no puede pedirlo.

# Why a plugin's port can't be opened. { $port } is such as TCP 24810, { $plugin } is the other plugin's name.
common-firewall-taken = { $port } ya lo usa { $plugin }, así que no se puede abrir también para este complemento.

# Why a plugin cannot open another port: { $max } is how many may be open.
